SM(269,{"n":"Genesis 40-41","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Genesis 40-41.mp3","d":2880.4,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.36,"So chapter 40."],[23.44,"Now it came to pass after these things."],[27.12,"So that's a quick way of saying some time passes."],[31.25,"Joseph spends some time in prison."],[34.21,"Which this is hard time beyond."],[39.7,"After these things, that the king of Egypt's chief cupbearer and the chief baker offended their lord the king of Egypt."],[47.54,"So Pharaoh was angry with his two eunuchs, the chief cupbearer and the chief baker."],[52.02,"Okay. So again, eunuch, see previous note."],[55.79,"These are officials."],[57.52,"So the cupbearer was an incredibly important trusted position."],[63.36,"Because you think, wow, he carried a cup around."],[66.0,"But no, this was this was the guy who tasted all of the drink that was going to be served to Pharaoh to make sure it wasn't poisoned."],[75.36,"And I don't mean make sure it wasn't poisoned, as in like he was carefully trained to sniff and detect poison, or to take tiny sips and detect poison by taste."],[86.24,"He would take a drink and they'd see if he'd die."],[90.37,"He would take a drink and they would watch."],[93.54,"Now, of course, why I say this had to be a trusted position is if somebody was going to try and poison Pharaoh, here's your ideal guy to do it."],[103.04,"So this had to be someone you deeply trusted."],[105.53,"Because it'd be very easy for him to take a drink and then slip something in and give it to Pharaoh."],[111.13,"So this had to be a very trusted position."],[113.31,"But you were also consenting to sort of be the guinea pick."],[116.37,"To be the buffer."],[118.13,"If someone did try to poison it, it was probably going to get you before it got him."],[123.41,"The baker, similarly."],[125.73,"So the fact that it's the two of them implies there must have been some incident where either someone tried to poison Pharaoh, or he thought Pharaoh paranoiacally thought someone was trying to poison him, maybe, and didn't trust them."],[143.91,"Remember, when you're when when you're a monarch who's worshipped as a god."],[148.65,"Everyone under you is subject to your whims all the time."],[152.38,"So he gets a wild hair, you know."],[154.22,"I don't like the way you looked at me yesterday."],[156.94,"Guess who's in prison for who knows how long."],[159.95,"Um so these two, but the baker obviously was also gonna be a trusted position because he's this isn't Baker, like, you know, he's making, you know, croissant and uh beignets, and bringing the bread."],[176.35,"This is he's making the bread every day."],[179.57,"So your primary food source for Pharaoh."],[182.71,"Again, gotta trust this guy, because if somebody's gonna try poisonous food."],[186.07,"Um so for whatever reason, we're not told exactly why"],[192.0,"Pharaoh gets mad at them or decides he doesn't trust them."],[195.36,"Throw them in the prison."],[197.04,"So they get thrown in the hole where Joseph is."],[202.56,"Verse 3, thus he put them in custody with the chief bodyguard of the prison, the place where Joseph was confined."],[209.2,"Then the chief jailer committed them to Joseph, and he attended them, so they were in custody for a while."],[216.24,"So he attended them."],[218.49,"This is the the jailer says, keep an eye on these two. who Pharaoh threw in here"],[227.69,"Then the king of Egypt's chief cupbearer,er the and the chief bak who were confined in prison, had a dream, both of them."],[235.33,"Each man's dream in one night, and each man's dream with its own interpretation."],[241.73,"Okay. So they each have a dream in the same night."],[247.19,"This idea of each man's dream, I mean they're they don't have the same dream."],[251.11,"They each have a dream."],[252.81,"In the same night."],[254.97,"Again, we mentioned this a little, but we'll reiterate a little now because this is about to become very pertinent here in the next couple chapters."],[262.73,"That dreams were understood in the ancient Near East in general to be the functioning of the news."],[273.71,"Uh, which is the capacity of a human being to see and comprehend the spiritual world functioning while you were asleep."],[285.23,"So they didn't think dreams were your imagination, or like we would hear today, your brain processing things from the day, or hallucinations, or however else we might look at dreams."],[298.19,"They looked at dreams as when you go to sleep and you dream, you are entering into the spiritual world."],[305.47,"And you are seeing things in the spiritual world, sort of the way that prophets would have visions."],[312.37,"And be able to see into the spiritual world."],[314.45,"The difference was a prophet could sort of do this as an activity."],[318.37,"So pagan prophets would do this usually through what we would call pharmacological means"],[326.01,"The word pharmacaea in Greek actually means sorcery."],[338.89,"Initiate an altered state of consciousness."],[341.93,"But a prophet was someone, a seer."],[345.42,"Someone who could do this sort of at will or regularly."],[349.58,"Whereas dreams. Sometimes you sleep and you don't dream."],[353.68,"Sometimes you sleep and you do dream."],[355.44,"Sometimes you don't remember dreams."],[356.88,"Sometimes you do."],[358.24,"So this was sort of not subject to the person."],[362.76,"You can't decide to dream."],[364.84,"Most people. If you could lose a dream, you could lose a dream."],[367.56,"But most people can't like decide I'm going to have a dream tonight."],[372.01,"Um, it's just something that happens to people."],[374.81,"But it was seen to be the same thing that those prophets and seers were doing."],[379.77,"It was just sort of working in the opposite direction."],[382.09,"Instead of a person deliberately entering into the spiritual world through some means."],[386.41,"This was the spiritual world sort of intruding into your heart, your mind while you're asleep."],[394.01,"So these dreams were taken very seriously for that reason"],[399.04,"It wasn't just like, oh hey, I had this weird dream, I had this funny dream."],[403.48,"Uh it was what, you know, some spiritual entity."],[408.98,"A god of spirit is trying to communicate something to me."],[412.9,"And this is the dream."],[414.26,"And so a person who could interpret dreams was sort of like a prophet or a seer."],[421.94,"In that they were able to sort of receive and translate spirit world language."],[430.02,"They were able to translate that visual language of visions and that kind of thing and explain what it meant, sort of decode the message that was being sent to the person who had the dream."],[441.7,"So this was a task that was usually performed by priests or prophets, seers."],[449.32,"In addition. We also talked about, though, how we have to understand that this is a step down from what we've seen before."],[457.88,"Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, God appears to them and talks to them in person."],[463.98,"Visually appears to them and stands there and talking."],[466.38,"Eight with Abraham."],[468.8,"We're not going to see that with Joseph."],[473.05,"So with Joseph, it's in this context of dreams."],[478.59,"And that's in part, we see this general kind of decline."],[483.79,"That's part of what's going to lead to that dispersion, this kind of decline as we go toward the end of the book of Genesis that is going to initiate why the Torah is given."],[493.53,"Why the commandments are given, why the law is given, as a guide."],[497.98,"Because on one hand, when we get into Exodus, we're going to have another man, we're going to have Moses, who's going to speak to God face to face again."],[507.23,"But everyone else in Israel isn't."],[511.47,"None of the other Israelites are."],[515.48,"They're going to have it mediated through Moses."],[518.76,"And then on an ongoing basis, mediated through a prophet."],[523.82,"Who God sends."],[526.51,"And so that's that's part of this transition, too, in terms of the move to dreams and their interpretations."],[532.67,"Verse 6 Okay."],[535.75,"So each of them has a dream."],[538.71,"So Joseph came into them in the morning and looked at them and saw they were troubled."],[544.49,"So he sees them in the morning, and both of them are troubled."],[548.57,"Why are they troubled?"],[549.83,"Like we wouldn't have a dream at night and be like, oh, I'm deeply troubled."],[552.72,"Maybe it was a horrible nightmare or something."],[554.56,"But right. They're trouble because they're like, I what does this mean?"],[558.18,"What am I am I supposed to do something?"],[560.18,"They found themselves in pretty bad straits."],[562.28,"They've been thrown in this hole."],[563.96,"They may very well die here in not that much time."],[567.72,"And now they have this dream."],[569.72,"Is this the way out?"],[570.92,"Is this condemnation?"],[572.78,"What is this?"],[576.66,"Verse 7. Thus he asked Pharaoh's eunuchs who are with him in the custody of his Lord, saying, Why do you look so sad today?"],[583.78,"So he said to him, We each had a dream, and there's no one to interpret it."],[588.42,"So they clearly talk to each other."],[590.84,"And that there's no one to interpret it means they're both stumped about their own and the other persons."],[596.05,"They have no idea."],[599.25,"And Joseph said to them, Do not interpretations belong to God, therefore relate them to me."],[607.41,"This is interesting, too."],[609.75,"He says, Interpretations belong to God."],[611.73,"He's expecting them again."],[613.01,"Notice he uses the word God."],[614.53,"He's expecting them to agree with this."],[617.27,"To say, oh, well, yeah, that's who the message is from."],[618.71,"message is The from the divine realm."],[619.11,"So yeah, that's how you would have to interpret it"],[626.25,"So he says, Tell them to me."],[628.17,"Verse 9. Then the chief cupbearer related his dream to Joseph and said to him, Behold, in my dream, a vine was before me, and in the vine were three branches."],[639.37,"It was as though it budded, its blossoms shot forth, and its clusters brought forth ripe grapes."],[646.41,"Then Pharaoh's cup was in my hand, and I took the grapes and pressed them into Pharaoh's cup, and placed the cup in Pharaoh's hand."],[655.21,"So he kind of sees this branch grow from the grapevine."],[660.26,"And it branched off in three directions, and then it buds, and then the buds turn into grapes."],[665.92,"And the grapes ripen, and he takes them and squeezes them into the cup and gives it to Pharaoh."],[671.12,"But he's probably sitting there thinking, okay, why three?"],[674.24,"Why? Right on right."],[680.0,"And Joseph said to him, This is the interpretation of it."],[682.88,"The three branches are three days."],[686.32,"Now, within three days, Pharaoh will remember your position and restore your office of chief cup-bearer, and you will put Pharaoh's cup in his hand according to the former manner when you were his cupbearer."],[699.28,"So he says, Here's what it means: in three days, he's gonna remember he threw you down here."],[705.34,"He will have changed his mind."],[707.18,"He will bring you back and give you your old trusted job back"],[713.54,"Verse 14, but remember me when it is well with you, and have mercy on me."],[718.98,"Make mention of me to Pharaoh and get me out of this prison."],[723.14,"For indeed I was stolen away from the land of the Hebrews, and I also have done nothing for them to put me into the dungeon."],[730.31,"So he's so confident, he's not guessing here."],[733.85,"So he says, Hey, in three days when you're up there, and you're what if Pharaoh's chief advice?"],[739.61,"Say something about me down here."],[741.21,"Everybody's forgotten me down here."],[742.73,"He's like, Look, I was abducted, sold into slavery."],[746.65,"I didn't do anything to end up down here."],[749.22,"I'm innocent. So hey, help me."],[750.82,"Right when you get a chance"],[752.14,"I've helped you out by interpreting this."],[754.06,"Help me out."],[756.46,"Verse 16. When the chief baker saw the interpretation was good, he said to Joseph."],[762.56,"So he says, Oh, okay, okay."],[765.76,"This is good."],[766.8,"Hey, here's mine."],[767.92,"Here's mine. I also had a dream, and there were three white baskets on my head."],[775.92,"And the uppermost basket were all kinds of baked goods for Pharaoh."],[779.92,"And the birds ate them out of the basket on my head."],[783.7,"So, you know, he's probably thinking, Oh, three baskets?"],[786.26,"Maybe in three days, I get out too."],[789.08,"The birds, they fly."],[790.12,"I'm gonna fly out of the prison."],[791.82,"Maybe something like that, Joseph?"],[793.91,"So Joseph answered and said, This is the interpretation of it."],[794.87,"The three baskets are three days"],[800.35,"Within three days, Pharaoh will lift off your head from you and hang you on a tree, and the birds will eat your flesh from you."],[807.79,"So that escalated quickly."],[812.46,"But Joseph's calling them like he sees them."],[814.64,"He's not sugarcoating it at all."],[817.81,"You're gonna get beheaded, and your body's gonna be hung on a tree and a cursed, and birds are gonna come and eat you."],[827.41,"d We we don't get a reaction from the baker."],[831.05,"Uh uh, so we don't know if it was absolute despair or if it was just, ah, this guy doesn't know what he's talking about."],[837.13,"Verse twenty We don't know."],[842.15,"Now it came to pass on the third day, which was Pharaoh's birthday, that he made a feast for all his servants, and he remembered the positions of his chief cupbearer and chief baker among his servants."],[853.59,"Then he restored the chief cupbearer to his position and he placed the cup in Pharaoh's hand."],[858.23,"But he hanged the chief baker as Joseph had interpreted to them."],[863.03,"Yet the chief cupbearer did not remember Joseph, but forgot him."],[868.48,"So exactly what he said would happen happens."],[871.92,"But now that things are better for the chief cupbearer."],[876.48,"Yeah, there's some weirdo foreigner in there who interpreted my dream."],[879.96,"But moving on."],[882.12,"Moving on. Back to life."],[885.32,"Like I've always like every time I've read the story, I've always been like, how could he just have we forgotten about him?"],[891.88,"Well, that's true, but I've also known a lot of people."],[897.41,"This is a pretty significant thing, Dream."],[899.67,"Because Farrow was mad at you, and this guy said you weren't gonna, you were gonna like it."],[903.51,"You don't you don't know anybody who's done well and made it big and who you helped out, and all of a sudden they don't they don't know who you are?"],[910.15,"Fair enough. Yeah."],[911.92,"That's that happens."],[913.7,"That's very human."],[915.7,"And very real."],[917.06,"You know? It never said the cupbearer was a great guy."],[923.14,"He doesn't forget him totally completely."],[924.02,"Chapter 41 Then it came to pass at the end of two full years."],[933.02,"So Joseph spends another two years living in that hole."],[938.54,"Forgotten about. And for two full years, if Pharaoh had a dream."],[944.86,"And behold, he stood by the river."],[948.3,"Suddenly there came up out of the river seven cows, fine-looking and fat, and they fed in the meadow."],[957.5,"Then behold, seven other cows came up after them out of the river, ugly and gaunt, and stood by the other cows on the bank of the river."],[967.1,"But the ugly and gaunt cows ate up the seven fine looking and fat cows."],[972.5,"So Pharaoh awoke."],[974.1,"So this is kind of a creepy, horrific dream."],[979.19,"Things coming out of rivers."],[982.12,"This is weird to us."],[984.26,"May I remember back when we were going through Revelation, things coming up out of the sea, and in Daniel, beasts have coming up out of the sea."],[992.42,"That's more people on the Mediterranean coast where things come out of the sea, like Greeks and that kind of thing."],[998.18,"When you're dealing with like Mesopotamians, where you've got the Tigris and Euphrates, or Egyptians, where you've got the Nile."],[1006.43,"Things come out of rivers."],[1008.96,"And so rivers in general, like underneath the river or underneath the sea, what gets called the abyss in Greek, underneath the sea."],[1018.78,"The bottom of the sea, the bottom of the river."],[1021.42,"This is the underworld."],[1025.68,"So this is what we would call supernatural."],[1028.16,"This is a divine realm, often a negative kind of divine realm, but not always negative."],[1036.98,"So, like in Babylonian stories, the seven sages who come and give knowledge to man come up out of the river."],[1046.82,"Then they're punished by the gods and imprisoned under the river."],[1049.55,"So there's this ambivalent kind of thing."],[1054.03,"So when the cows come up out of the river, that in itself is it that is again this sort of divine port."],[1062.97,"These cows, are coming out of the divine realm."],[1066.19,"There is some message here that these cows represent and are bringing."],[1070.11,"So there's seven of them who are good, healthy, chubby cows."],[1076.35,"And then there's seven that are sickly, and look like they're about to drop dead."],[1082.05,"But the sickly ones then eat, like kill and eat."],[1087.35,"And this isn't cartoon eat."],[1089.19,"This isn't like, this is the idea here is this is more horror movie, sickly gaunt zombie cows. tear into and devour"],[1100.5,"So you can understand why he would suddenly wake up and be disturbed, after seeing this."],[1104.86,"What does this mean?"],[1106.06,"But clearly, especially with the river symbolism, this is something, again, that's in this divine sphere."],[1113.52,"So this is this this is some kind of important message."],[1116.88,"Pharaoh would understand."],[1118.8,"Verse 5. He slept and dreamed a second time, so he goes back to sleep."],[1123.2,"Has another dream."],[1126.16,"Suddenly seven ears of corn came up on one stalk, plump and good."],[1135.44,"Then behold, seven ears of corn, thin and blighted by the east wind, sprang up after them."],[1140.56,"But the seven thin ears of corn devoured the seven plump and full years"],[1146.6,"So Pharaoh awoke and indeed it was a dream."],[1149.33,"So he wakes up again."],[1151.09,"So what's the significance of the east wind as opposed to like wouldn't like a north?"],[1156.37,"Like north is usually where bad things come from."],[1158.87,"But this is remember where we're in Egypt."],[1162.24,"So Nile River flows south to north."],[1166.4,"East is the desert."],[1168.88,"So this is dry desert wind blows in and like shrivels them up."],[1172.9,"Dries them up."],[1175.14,"So a similar but not identical."],[1178.12,"Kind of kind of symbol to the cows."],[1181.8,"Cannibalistic corn. Yes, cannibal corn."],[1186.0,"It's like attack of the killer tomatoes, but it's corn."],[1190.96,"It has the juice."],[1193.12,"So we're saying, now it came to pass in the morning that his spirit was troubled."],[1197.36,"And he sent and called for all the interpreters of Egypt and all its wise men."],[1202.57,"So he calls in."],[1204.39,"The people, the wise men and stuff who this is talking about."],[1206.79,"Wise men. Magi is a Persian thing."],[1209.47,"This is. So these are."],[1211.31,"I think we've mentioned this already."],[1213.63,"These are like the magicians, quote unquote, who are going to show up in Exodus in Egypt."],[1218.91,"Uh, these are mostly what were what are called by Egyptologists lector priests."],[1224.35,"It's lecter, not Hannibal Lecter."],[1226.43,"We're talking about cannibal.nibal corn, so just to be clear, we're not talking about like Han Lector"],[1231.27,"Lector is in Latin for a reader."],[1235.25,"They are literate."],[1237.65,"And so this was the most important cast of priests in Egypt."],[1243.17,"Because as I mentioned, we are at least in the Middle Kingdom."],[1248.93,"Really past the Middle Kingdom with Joseph."],[1252.37,"Um we are probably approaching the new kingdom already in Egypt."],[1256.61,"So there's an old and a middle kingdom behind this."],[1259.26,"Egypt is already ancient."],[1262.62,"There are texts and inscriptions, the ritual texts, the religious texts and inscriptions go back a thousand years already."],[1275.3,"And so the responsibility of this cast of priests was to be able to read them."],[1281.22,"To be able to read them and not only read them, but read, interpret, and apply them."],[1288.18,"So situation arises."],[1291.86,"There is some divine import to it."],[1295.3,"What do we do?"],[1296.18,"How do we respond?"],[1298.1,"What kind of sacrifices do we offer?"],[1300.82,"Etc. etc. we consult with these lector priests, they consult with the scrolls, with the ancient temple inscriptions."],[1309.22,"They get back to you and tell you: here is what we need to do."],[1313.16,"And then we do it."],[1315.48,"So. they are the preservers of this knowledge and the interpreters and appliers of this knowledge"],[1322.96,"Pharaoh immediately says, get them all in here."],[1326.34,"And when it says summons them all, there are various temples in various cities to various gods."],[1332.92,"So he he's get me everybody."],[1335.34,"Anybody who knows anything."],[1337.91,"Because I need to know what this means."],[1339.83,"I need to know what these dreams mean."],[1341.83,"So he rounds them all up."],[1343.51,"And it's not, you have to remember, I mean, literacy is unbelievably rare until very recently."],[1351.27,"I know I've said this before in the Bible study, but in World War One, the U.S."],[1357.19,"Army considered you literate. if you could sign your name instead of just putting an X"],[1365.95,"So, and the literacy rate then was something like 18 to 20%."],[1376.19,"So that's not 18 to 20% could actually read books."],[1380.99,"That was 18 to 20% could sign their name."],[1385.87,"World War One, 20th century."],[1389.15,"Um but in the ancient world, you have to remember, especially, for example, in Egypt now, they don't have an alphabet."],[1399.47,"Things are written in hieratic."],[1402.67,"There are hundreds of symbols."],[1407.43,"And we're talking about texts written over hundreds of years."],[1411.59,"Where symbols are coming in and going out and the interpretation of them is changing."],[1417.29,"We're talking about pictographic language."],[1419.61,"So being able to read is this is an elite caste."],[1424.09,"So these are these are pharaohs, not just they have this religious significance, but these are the top scholars, these are the top everything."],[1433.83,"In Egypt. Pharaoh rounds them all up."],[1437.83,"This Pharaoh told them his dreams, but there was no one who could interpret them for Pharaoh."],[1443.19,"And this doesn't mean they all stood around stomped."],[1445.99,"I'm sure some of them had ideas."],[1447.87,"I'm sure some of them offered some kind of ideas, but none that satisfied Pharaoh."],[1454.43,"Where Pharaoh heard it and said, That's clearly it."],[1458.64,"Then the cupbearer spoke to Pharaoh, saying, I remember my sin this day."],[1462.8,"What does that mean?"],[1463.6,"I remember my error."],[1464.8,"Hey, you know what?"],[1465.84,"I just remembered, I messed up."],[1469.76,"When Pharaoh was angry with his servants and put me in custody in the house of the chief bodyguard, both myself and the chief baker, we each had a dream in one night, both he and I, each had a dream regarding himself."],[1482.88,"Now there was with us a young Hebrew servant, Reed slave, of the chief bodyguard, and we related our dreams to him, and he interpreted them for us, and it came to pass just as he interpreted for us."],[1494.76,"So it happened, he restored me to my office, but he hanged him, meaning the baker."],[1505.32,"Cutbear, close advisor, says, Man, I messed up."],[1508.92,"I was supposed to remember this guy."],[1512.25,"He says, When I was two years ago."],[1515.01,"When I was briefly in in prison, there was this Hebrew slave, this foreigner."],[1520.26,"Slave down there."],[1521.38,"And when we had dreams, he interpreted them, and he interpreted them exactly correctly."],[1526.76,"So maybe check with him."],[1528.44,"Maybe he can do something for you, King."],[1532.44,"He's at least close by."],[1537.18,"Verse 14 then Pharaoh sent and called Joseph, and they brought him quickly out of the dungeon, and he shaved, changed his clothing, and came to Pharaoh."],[1546.46,"So, in terms of changing his clothing, from my description earlier of what the prison was like, that should be obvious."],[1552.0,"Takes off the filthy rags, and gets cleaned up."],[1555.21,"But we also mentioned, I think, at one point at least, Egyptian uh the Egyptian obsession with hygiene."],[1562.97,"Uh, in terms of the pharaohs, in terms of the upper class."],[1567.53,"So in the Nile River Valley and Delta, especially, there was a massive lice problem."],[1576.25,"Problem with lice, fleas. ticks, etc"],[1581.57,"And so one of the ways that the upper class dealt with this was by shaving."],[1588.05,"And you've probably seen this in documentaries and in even movies with ancient Egypt."],[1593.25,"Shaving doesn't just mean men didn't grow beards."],[1596.15,"They shaved everything."],[1597.19,"They shaved off their eyebrows, they shaved their heads, both men and women."],[1603.11,"Uh everything. We're completely shaved."],[1606.25,"And then they would wear sort of ornamental beards."],[1610.71,"Use makeup to draw in eyebrows."],[1614.05,"Wear wigs. Artificial wigs, um, all to control lice, fleas, ticks."],[1622.88,"Um, so if he's gonna come before Pharaoh, Pharaoh doesn't want filthy foreigner carrying who knows what out of the prison to boot."],[1632.77,"So they not only give him some clean clothes and wash him up, but they also shave him."],[1638.87,"They shave everything."],[1640.55,"So he's not bringing anything bad into Pharaoh's presence."],[1647.27,"Verse 15 Thus Pharaoh said to Joseph, I had a dream, and there's no one who can interpret it."],[1653.27,"But I heard it said of you that you can understand a dream to interpret it."],[1658.71,"So Joseph answered Pharaoh, saying, It is not in me, God will give Pharaoh an answer of peace."],[1662.95,"an answer of peace So, what does mean?"],[1664.15,"Because he's not"],[1667.07,"Not, oh, I'm sure it's going to be good."],[1670.65,"Remember the whole baker thing."],[1672.33,"It's an answer of peace, meaning an answer that will satisfy you."],[1677.66,"God will give me an answer where you will hear it and you will say, Yes, that's it."],[1681.52,"Because the other answers he's gotten have been unsatisfactory."],[1688.88,"Verse 17. Then Pharaoh said to Joseph, Behold, in my dream I stood on the bank of the river, meaning the Nile, obviously."],[1695.68,"Suddenly seven cows came up out of the river, fine looking and fat, and they fed in the meadow."],[1701.44,"Then behold, seven other cows came up after them, poor and very ugly and gaunt, such ugliness as I have never seen in all the land of Egypt."],[1709.8,"And the gaunt and ugly cows ate up the first seven, the fat cows."],[1714.92,"When they had eaten them, no one would have known they had eaten them, for they were just as ugly as at the beginning."],[1721.16,"So I awoke and fell asleep again."],[1723.74,"So we say it's not like they got fat eating the fat cows."],[1727.02,"They were still gaunt and skeletal and twenty-two again."],[1738.54,"Then behold, seven ears of corn withered thin and blighted by the east wind sprang up after them."],[1744.3,"But the thin ears of corn devoured the seven good ears."],[1748.14,"So I told all this to the interpreters, but there was no one who could explain it to me."],[1754.02,"So he lays it out, he says, no one could explain it to me."],[1758.9,"Verse 25. Then Joseph said to Pharaoh, The dreams of Pharaoh are one."],[1764.58,"God has shown Pharaoh what he is about to do."],[1768.02,"So notice it doesn't say Joseph went and deliberated."],[1770.9,"He said, I'll be back in the prison."],[1772.42,"Give me a couple days."],[1774.96,"Because we're supposed to understand."],[1778.02,"Again, this is an image of the change in prophecy."],[1780.43,"Moses sees God face to face, but then the prophets, are speaking for God."],[1785.99,"This isn't something Joseph comes up with and is inspired in some vague way."],[1790.23,"God is giving this to him in the same way he gave the dream to Pharaoh."],[1799.15,"The seven good cows are seven years, and the seven good ears of corn are seven years."],[1804.11,"The dreams are one."],[1805.87,"But the seven thin and ugly cows that came up after them are seven years, and the seven empty heads blighted by the east wind are seven years of famine."],[1815.79,"This is the thing I have spoken to Pharaoh."],[1817.95,"God has shown Pharaoh what he is about to do."],[1820.75,"So he says, in this dream, God is showing you what he's about to do."],[1829.55,"Indeed, seven years of great plenty will come throughout all the land of Egypt, but after them, seven years of famine will arise, and all the plenty will be forgotten in the land of Egypt, and the famine will deplete the land."],[1842.95,"So the plenty will not be known in the land because of the famine following, for it will be very severe."],[1850.23,"So he's saying the famine is going to be way worse than the plenty is good."],[1856.25,"Such that it's going to devour all of that prosperity."],[1873.05,"So meaning, what does that mean?"],[1875.69,"That means this isn't God calling you to like repent."],[1880.27,"This isn't like a threat."],[1882.43,"It's you got it twice to confirm this is going to happen."],[1887.51,"Regardless. This is what is about to happen over the next fourteen years."],[1896.84,"Now, therefore, let Pharaoh select a sensible and intelligent man and set him over the land of Egypt."],[1903.58,"So this is Joseph making a proposal now."],[1908.3,"Let Pharaoh do this and let him appoint governors over the land to collect one fifth of the produce of the land of Egypt in the seven plentiful years."],[1919.18,"So let them gather all the food of the seven good years that are coming, and store up grain under Pharaoh's authority, and let them keep food in the cities."],[1927.74,"That food shall then be as a reserve in the land for the seven coming years of famine in the land of Egypt, that the land may not perish during the famine."],[1938.26,"So he says, Take one fifth, take twenty percent during the good years when there's abundance, store it up."],[1947.16,"And then you'll have surplus that you can use during the seven bad years."],[1953.08,"So God's shown you what he's going to do over the next fourteen years."],[1955.48,"You can now prepare."],[1957.24,"So you need to get someone you trust to be in charge of this, and he needs to have people working under him in all the different cities to make sure that this happens and things get stored properly."],[1971.16,"Verse 37. Now, this advice was good in the eyes of Pharaoh. and in the eyes of all his servants"],[1977.76,"Thus Pharaoh said to his servants, Can we find such a man as this who has the Spirit of God in him?"],[1985.14,"So he recognizes immediately, yes, this is what the vision means."],[1990.12,"This answer satisfies him and gives him peace."],[1994.36,"And so he says, and and this is good advice."],[1997.97,"This is a good way to handle that."],[1999.65,"And so when he says, can we find such a man as this?"],[2002.45,"Because Joseph said, You need to find right a good and intelligent man."],[2005.97,"And he's saying to everybody, Hey, is there any guy better than this guy?"],[2010.79,"Who's going to be more wise and more able to administrate this?"],[2015.51,"Then Pharaoh said to Joseph, Inasmuch as as God has shown you all this, there is no one as sensible and as intelligent you."],[2021.95,"You shall be over my house, and all my people shall be ruled according to your word."],[2027.07,"Only in regard to the throne will I be greater than you."],[2031.39,"So Pharaoh said to Joseph, See, I have set you over all the land of Egypt."],[2036.59,"So now this is sort of like the Potiphar situation, but with Pharaoh of all Egypt rather than just Potiphar and his household."],[2045.73,"So Joseph's kind of like a region."],[2047.97,"Yeah. Joseph is given these sweeping powers because there's an emergency coming."],[2054.13,"So he's sort of given these emergency powers."],[2056.53,"You're gonna be in charge to make sure all this happens."],[2059.49,"And so you could go and speak on Pharaoh's authority."],[2062.81,"When you go to a city, you could say, Hey, on Pharaoh's authority, we're collecting this grain, we're storing it here, this guy's in charge of it for this city."],[2071.83,"He's giving Joseph those powers to make this happen."],[2081.35,"Yeah. Then it's the apotifier and then the prison keeper now."],[2090.06,"Because he's stayed faithful through all this."],[2093.84,"He's stayed faithful to God through all this."],[2097.44,"Which has been more downs than ups so far."],[2100.16,"This is definitely an up."],[2103.12,"Yeah. But he's he's stayed faithful."],[2107.53,"Um, and that faithfulness, just like with Abraham."],[2112.03,"The faithfulness is what God honored."],[2115.17,"As him being a righteous man."],[2117.33,"The same thing with Joseph."],[2121.89,"Notice something though, too."],[2125.33,"Notice something though, too."],[2127.57,"Um, because this is important."],[2132.73,"Uh this what is God doing here through Joseph?"],[2139.53,"He's saving Egypt."],[2142.73,"He's saving Egypt."],[2145.89,"Through Joseph. Remember the pattern, one of the patterns of the promises to Abraham, remember, is all the nations will bless themselves in you."],[2158.22,"That all the nations will be blessed through him."],[2161.18,"So the promises to Abraham and his seed are not exclusivist promises."],[2167.5,"It's not you instead of everybody else."],[2171.18,"It's you and through you, everybody else."],[2178.32,"And so here's a nation, Egypt."],[2182.3,"A pagan nation, a Gentile nation."],[2185.24,"But they're being blessed, they're being saved through Joseph."],[2189.24,"And through Joseph's faithfulness to God."],[2190.36,"Because those things go hand in hand"],[2196.32,"This is another part of this prologue to the rest of the Torah."],[2203.12,"Because in Exodus, God is going to say to them that He created Israel as a nation to be a kingdom of priests."],[2210.56,"Priests to who?"],[2214.24,"The nations. But for Israel to do that, for the nations to be blessed through Israel, Israel has to be faithful to God."],[2226.56,"That's how it works."],[2227.44,"And so Joseph here is an example of that."],[2238.88,"Verse 42, then Pharaoh took the signet ring off his hand and put it on Joseph's hand."],[2244.08,"And he clothed him in garments of fine linen and put a gold chain around his neck."],[2249.84,"Why is the signet ring important?"],[2251.44,"Well, this is the sign, not just a sign of his authority, like, hey, look, I've got Pharaoh's ring, but you use that to seal documents."],[2260.05,"So effectively, in modern terms, when Joseph signs off on something, Pharaoh is signing off on something."],[2268.39,"He's got Pharaoh's signature, essentially."],[2271.25,"To be able to use that authority."],[2277.09,"Then he had him ride in the second of his chariots, and they cried out before him, bow the knee"],[2283.29,"So he set him over all the land of Egypt."],[2286.57,"Pharaoh also said to Joseph, I am Pharaoh, and without your consent, no man may lift his hand or foot in all the land of Egypt."],[2295.53,"Then Pharaoh called Joseph's name Zaphnath Penea."],[2302.33,"And he gave him as a wife Asenath, the daughter of Potipharah."],[2309.29,"There's our second Potiphar, even though it's transliterated differently for reasons unknown."],[2315.85,"The Orthodox study Bible."],[2318.01,"Priest of On."],[2319.85,"On is a city."],[2321.93,"It's Heliopolis. Obviously, Heliopolis is Greek"],[2323.49,"It's later going to be called Heliopolis."],[2328.93,"They called it Heliopolis because On was a city dedicated to the sun god Re."],[2336.77,"And so, yes, Joseph marries the daughter of a pagan priest."],[2345.09,"And this is going to be a subject of much interest."],[2349.03,"We'll get into the quote unquote ethnic makeup in modern terms of Israel a lot when we get into Exodus."],[2357.67,"But the fact that she's the daughter of a pagan priest becomes a subject of much fascination."],[2365.75,"And so there is a famous apocryphal Old Testament work, story of Joseph and Asenath, that is about this."],[2375.47,"And is essentially, again, this is put in modern terms, but essentially it's a melding of a romance and the story of her conversion to worshiping Yahweh."],[2393.79,"It was super popular with early Christians as a read."],[2398.59,"Was never considered to be put into the Bible."],[2400.72,"Was never used as scripture by anybody."],[2403.12,"But was very popular."],[2405.44,"And is alluded to at the end of St."],[2408.64,"Luke's Gospel. I'll just drop as a seed thing."],[2413.4,"But do you know what uh the translation of Joseph's Egyptian name is?"],[2419.96,"Oh, Zaphanath. Zaphanat."],[2423.72,"It's like Zaphanat."],[2426.6,"Uh Panea. So it's a it's again a good there's theories as to what you have is Egyptian name, transliterated into Hebrew, transliterated into Greek."],[2445.28,"s T transranliterated here."],[2447.08,"So there's no real translation."],[2449.0,"It's kind of, it's kind of unclear, but he gives him an Egyptian name."],[2454.26,"So the idea is he's sort of being adopted into Pharaoh's household."],[2460.75,"Um. Yeah. Yes."],[2465.71,"And that's part of the deliberate parallel."],[2467.95,"He's sort of being adopted into his family."],[2470.75,"And the kind of favor Pharaoh, Pharaoh puts these garments on him."],[2475.05,"Think about Jacob, his father, giving him the coat."],[2479.99,"This is sort of right, this adoption idea."],[2484.48,"And so that includes having an Egyptian name."],[2489.92,"Translate. I mean, like, there's theories."],[2493.84,"Well, Osis means what drawn out of the water."],[2496.72,"It doesn't actually, but we'll get to that in Exodus."],[2498.48,"Yes, that is a that is a bogus uh etymology"],[2505.32,"Um yeah, I I won't go into that too much now because we will talk about that very early on in Exodus, and we're we're not that far from Exodus, frankly."],[2515.32,"Um but yeah, so Moses' Egyptian name was probably included more than Moses."],[2525.56,"Because Moses means child, and was usually affixed in Egyptian names to the name of an Egyptian god."],[2536.12,"So we'll talk about what he gets named, but it's also very possible that there's the name of an Egyptian god that's been dropped out to just leave the Moses part."],[2549.12,"But Ramses is Ra or Re plus Moses."],[2555.04,"Pharaoh Thut Moses is Thoth plus Moses, because Moses means child."],[2561.12,"So like child over son of Ra, child over son of Thoth."],[2567.36,"And his and and I'm teasing stuff, but uh strangely enough, his sister Miriam, who is not adopted by Pharaoh, also has an Egyptian name that actually has the name of a pagan god in it."],[2583.68,"Miriamni means beloved of Amun in the Egyptian."],[2588.48,"So But I will get back to you next time with some of the I'll just throw you some of the theories, and you can decide if any of them are satisfactory about Zaphadath Padea."],[2602.04,"I don't find any of them super satisfactory, is basically what I mean."],[2608.28,"Okay. Verse 46."],[2610.52,"Now Joseph was 30 years old when he stood before Pharaoh, king of Egypt."],[2615.24,"Then Joseph went out from the presence of Pharaoh and went throughout all the land of Egypt."],[2621.56,"Now in the seven plentiful years, the ground brought forth abundantly."],[2625.58,"So now we're at now we're at 37."],[2627.66,"He's 37 years old."],[2629.9,"So it says he went out and went to Egypt."],[2632.22,"We're kind of getting the montage now."],[2634.68,"Of him over these seven years going around and setting up the warehouses for grain and getting everything set up and ready."],[2642.36,"Now in the seven plentiful years the ground brought forth abundantly."],[2645.72,"So he gathered up all the food of the seven years of prosperity in the land of Egypt and stored the food in the cities."],[2651.88,"He laid up in every city the food of the fields that surrounded them."],[2655.88,"Joseph gathered very much grain as the sand of the sea until he stopped counting, for it was immeasurable."],[2662.54,"So eventually they're just like, nah, just keep taking 20% and storing it up."],[2666.54,"Don't bother weighing it all out."],[2671.63,"Now two sons were born to Joseph before the years of famine came."],[2675.79,"Whom Asanath, the daughter of Potipharah, priest of Own bore to him"],[2681.59,"Joseph called the name of his firstborn Manasseh."],[2685.11,"For God has made me forget all the troubles in all my father's house."],[2689.11,"Manasseh means forgetfulness."],[2693.51,"And the name of the second he called Ephraim."],[2696.39,"For God has caused me to be fruitful in the land of my humiliation."],[2702.63,"And Ephraim means fruitfulness, fruits."],[2710.67,"So he gives them what are Hebrew names, at least as it's presented here."],[2715.37,"U,h not Egyptian names."],[2717.93,"I guess right, Manasseh here is the firstborn."],[2720.41,"Uh, switcheroo is gonna happen as usual in chapter 48"],[2726.29,"But um, so he has these these two sons."],[2731.57,"Then the seven years of plenty in the land of Egypt ended, and the seven years of famine began to come, as Joseph said, the famine was in all lands, but in all the land of Egypt there was bread."],[2745.63,"So this isn't just a localized thing in Egypt."],[2748.35,"This is over sort of the whole ancient Near East, at least the Levant was included."],[2754.67,"This is widespread, but because of the dream, because of Joseph's preparation, they have food in Egypt."],[2764.19,"So when all the land of Egypt was famished, the people cried to Pharaoh for bread."],[2764.59,"all the Then Pharaoh said to Egyptians, Go to Joseph, whatever he says to you, do."],[2773.41,"So Joseph is not only in charge of the whole program to store it up."],[2778.21,"Now, once the famine starts, he's in charge of the distribution in all of these cities."],[2788.05,"By the way, people tend to emphasize the fact that he's honored and he has the nice clothes and the goal that but he's also working hard."],[2796.34,"And this is more of that faithfulness."],[2798.62,"is This this is where he finds himself now."],[2800.58,"So he's dedicated to it."],[2802.42,"He's faithful. He's working hard and accomplishing this."],[2807.71,"Famine was over all the face of the earth."],[2808.59,"And Joseph opened all the storehouses and sold to the Egyptians"],[2814.23,"Then all countries also came to Joseph in Egypt to buy grain because the famine was severe in all the earth."],[2819.91,"Now what's being translated, earth, there actually means land."],[2823.91,"So all the land."],[2825.13,"It's not literally saying like people are coming from China."],[2829.35,"The famine went to China."],[2830.87,"But this is the neighboring countries are coming to Egypt."],[2835.45,"To say, hey."],[2837.31,"You're the only ones who are who are prepared."],[2840.67,"And this, of course, as you can see on the page, is setting up for a reunion that we'll talk about next time."],[2850.11,"So we'll wrap up here for tonight."],[2851.63,"So thank you, everybody"],[2852.63,"We did three chapters."],[2857.99,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2865.35,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancient faith dot com."],[2870.71,"That's wholecounsel at ancient faith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.36,"lv":2,"h":"40:1-4 - Cupbearer and baker in prison","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Genesis 40</b>: \"after these things\" = time passes; Joseph in prison - \"hard time\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:1-2</b>: Pharaoh's <b>chief cupbearer</b> and <b>chief baker</b> offended the king; \"eunuchs\" = <b>officials</b> (see previous note)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Cupbearer</b> = incredibly trusted position</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>tasted all of Pharaoh's drink</b> - not sniffing or tiny sips: \"he would take a drink and they'd see if he'd <b>die</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">ideal poisoner → had to be <b>deeply trusted</b></li><li class=\"d1\">also the \"<b>guinea pig</b>\", the buffer - poison would get you before him</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Baker</b> likewise: not croissants and beignets but <b>daily bread</b> = Pharaoh's primary food source</li><li class=\"d0\">Both jailed → some <b>incident</b> - real poison attempt, or Pharaoh <b>paranoid</b></li><li class=\"d1\">monarch worshipped as a god: everyone under him subject to <b>whims</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I don't like the way you looked at me yesterday\" → prison \"for who knows how long\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:3-4</b>: put in custody with the chief of the guard, where Joseph was; jailer <b>committed them to Joseph</b> - \"keep an eye on these two\"</li></ul>"},{"t":227.69,"lv":2,"h":"40:5 - Dreams in the ancient Near East","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:5</b>: each had a dream <b>in one night</b>, each with its own interpretation</li><li class=\"d0\">Reiterating - \"very pertinent\" in the next chapters</li><li class=\"d0\">Ancient Near East: dreams = functioning of the <b>nous</b></li><li class=\"d1\">nous = capacity to <b>see and comprehend the spiritual world</b>, working while asleep</li><li class=\"d1\">not imagination, not \"brain processing the day,\" not hallucination</li><li class=\"d1\">you <b>enter the spiritual world</b>, like a prophet's visions</li><li class=\"d0\">Prophet/seer vs dreamer</li><li class=\"d1\">prophet can do it <b>as an activity</b>; pagan prophets via <b>pharmacological means</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Greek <i>pharmakeia</i> = <b>sorcery</b>; induces altered state</li><li class=\"d1\">dreams <b>not subject to the person</b> - can't decide to dream, remember, etc.</li><li class=\"d1\">same thing, <b>opposite direction</b>: spiritual world <b>intruding</b> on your mind</li><li class=\"d0\">Taken very seriously: \"some spiritual entity is trying to communicate\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Dream interpreter</b> = like a prophet - <b>decodes spirit-world language</b>; usually <b>priests, prophets, seers</b></li></ul>"},{"t":449.32,"lv":3,"h":"A step down from face to face","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Step down: <b>Abraham, Isaac, Jacob</b> - God appeared and <b>talked in person</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not with Joseph - <b>dreams</b> instead</li><li class=\"d0\">Part of a general <b>decline</b> toward the end of Genesis</li><li class=\"d1\">leads to the <b>dispersion</b></li><li class=\"d1\">initiates why the <b>Torah, commandments, law</b> are given - \"as a guide\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Exodus</b>: <b>Moses</b> again speaks to God <b>face to face</b>; other Israelites don't</li><li class=\"d1\">mediated through Moses, then ongoing through <b>a prophet God sends</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Dreams and interpretation = part of this transition</li></ul>"},{"t":532.67,"lv":2,"h":"40:6-8 - \"Interpretations belong to God\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:6</b>: Joseph sees them in the morning, <b>troubled</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just a bad dream: \"what does this mean? am I supposed to do something?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">already in dire straits - <b>way out, or condemnation?</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:7-8</b>: \"Why do you look so sad today?\" - \"no one to interpret it\" - both stumped</li><li class=\"d0\">Joseph: \"<b>Do not interpretations belong to God?</b> Tell them to me\"</li><li class=\"d1\">says <b>God</b> (not the Lord) - expects them to <b>agree</b></li><li class=\"d1\">message is from the <b>divine realm</b></li></ul>"},{"t":628.17,"lv":2,"h":"40:9-15 - Cupbearer's dream","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:9-11</b>: <b>vine</b>, <b>three branches</b>, buds, blossoms, ripe clusters</li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh's cup in hand; <b>pressed grapes</b> into it; gave it to Pharaoh</li><li class=\"d1\">\"why <b>three</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:12-13</b>: three branches = <b>three days</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh will <b>remember</b> your position, <b>restore</b> your office</li><li class=\"d1\">he changes his mind → <b>old trusted job back</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:14-15</b>: \"<b>remember me</b> when it is well with you... have mercy... get me out\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"stolen away from the land of the Hebrews\"; \"done nothing... to put me into the dungeon\"</li><li class=\"d1\">confident, <b>not guessing</b>; \"I was abducted, sold into slavery... I'm <b>innocent</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I've helped you out. Help me out.\"</li></ul>"},{"t":756.46,"lv":2,"h":"40:16-19 - Baker's dream","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:16</b>: baker sees interpretation was <b>good</b> - \"here's mine\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:16-17</b>: <b>three white baskets</b> on my head; top one all baked goods for Pharaoh; <b>birds ate</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\">he's likely thinking: three baskets = three days out; \"<b>birds fly</b>, I'll fly out of prison\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:18-19</b>: three baskets = three days</li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh will <b>lift off your head</b> and <b>hang you on a tree</b>; birds eat your flesh</li><li class=\"d1\">\"that escalated quickly\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Joseph \"calling them like he sees them\" - <b>not sugarcoating</b></li><li class=\"d1\">beheaded, body hung on a tree = <b>cursed</b>, birds eat it</li><li class=\"d0\">No reaction from the baker - despair, or \"this guy doesn't know what he's talking about\"?</li></ul>"},{"t":842.15,"lv":2,"h":"40:20-23 - Fulfillment; forgotten","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:20-22</b>: <b>third day</b> = <b>Pharaoh's birthday</b>; feast for all servants</li><li class=\"d1\">he remembered both - <b>cupbearer restored</b>, <b>baker hanged</b> - \"exactly what he said would happen happens\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>40:23</b>: the cupbearer <b>did not remember Joseph, but forgot him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"some weirdo foreigner... but moving on\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: how could he forget? - Fr S: \"I've also known a lot of people\"</li><li class=\"d1\">someone you helped who made it big and <b>doesn't know you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"very human and very real\"; text <b>never said the cupbearer was a great guy</b></li></ul>"},{"t":924.02,"lv":2,"h":"41:1-4 - Pharaoh's first dream","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Chapter 41</b>: \"end of <b>two full years</b>\" - Joseph another two years in the hole, <b>forgotten</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:1-4</b>: by the <b>river</b>: <b>seven fat cows</b> come up, feed in the meadow</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>seven ugly, gaunt cows</b> come up; <b>eat</b> the fat ones; Pharaoh wakes</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Creepy, horrific\" - things out of rivers</li></ul>"},{"t":984.26,"lv":3,"h":"Things coming out of the river","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Parallels: <b>Revelation</b>, <b>Daniel</b> - beasts out of the <b>sea</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Mediterranean people (<b>Greeks</b>) = sea; <b>Mesopotamia</b> (Tigris, Euphrates), <b>Egypt</b> (Nile) = rivers</li><li class=\"d0\">Under river or sea = the <b>abyss</b> (Greek) = <b>underworld</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"supernatural\" = <b>divine realm</b>: often negative, not always</li><li class=\"d1\">Babylonian <b>seven sages</b> come up from the river with knowledge → punished, <b>imprisoned under the river</b></li><li class=\"d1\">so <b>ambivalent</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Cows from the river = <b>divine portent</b>; carry a message</li><li class=\"d0\">Gaunt cows <b>kill and eat</b> - \"not cartoon eat\" - \"horror movie, <b>sickly gaunt zombie cows</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh would understand it as <b>important</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1118.8,"lv":2,"h":"41:5-8 - Second dream; the wise men","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:5-7</b>: <b>seven plump ears</b> on one stalk; <b>seven thin ears blighted by the east wind</b> devour them; Pharaoh wakes</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>East wind</b>: Nile flows south to north; <b>east = desert</b> → dry wind <b>shrivels</b></li><li class=\"d1\">similar, not identical, to the cows - \"<b>cannibal corn</b>... attack of the killer tomatoes, but it's corn\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:8</b>: spirit troubled; summons all <b>interpreters</b> and <b>wise men</b> of Egypt</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Magi</b> = Persian; these = the \"<b>magicians</b>\" of <b>Exodus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">mostly <b>lector priests</b> - Latin <i>lector</i> = <b>reader</b> - \"not Hannibal Lecter\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1237.65,"lv":3,"h":"The lector priests","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Most important caste of priests - <b>literate</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Joseph's time: past the <b>Middle Kingdom</b>, near the <b>New Kingdom</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ritual/religious texts and inscriptions already ~<b>1000 years old</b></li><li class=\"d1\">job: <b>read, interpret and apply</b> them</li><li class=\"d0\">Process: sign of divine import → consult lector priests → they consult <b>scrolls and temple inscriptions</b> → \"here's what we do\" → we do it</li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh: \"get them all in here\" - temples in <b>various cities to various gods</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Literacy rarity</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>WWI</b> US Army: literate = could <b>sign your name</b>; ~<b>18-20%</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Egypt: <b>no alphabet</b>; <b>hieratic</b>, hundreds of symbols, pictographic, changing over centuries</li><li class=\"d1\">→ reading = <b>elite caste</b>; top scholars</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:8b</b>: no one could interpret - not all stumped; ideas offered, <b>none satisfied</b> Pharaoh</li></ul>"},{"t":1458.64,"lv":2,"h":"41:9-13 - The cupbearer remembers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:9</b>: \"I remember <b>my sin</b> this day\" = \"I just remembered, I messed up\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:10-13</b>: Pharaoh angry; <b>custody</b> with captain of the guard</li><li class=\"d1\">\"young <b>Hebrew slave</b>\" interpreted our dreams; <b>exactly correct</b>; restored me, hanged him</li><li class=\"d0\">\"He's at least close by\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1537.18,"lv":2,"h":"41:14-16 - Joseph shaved and brought to Pharaoh","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:14</b>: brought <b>quickly</b> from the dungeon; <b>shaved</b>, changed clothes</li><li class=\"d1\">filthy rags off - obvious from the prison</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Egyptian obsession with hygiene</b> (pharaohs, upper class)</li><li class=\"d1\">Nile Valley and Delta: massive <b>lice, fleas, ticks</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they <b>shaved everything</b> - eyebrows, heads, <b>men and women</b></li><li class=\"d1\">then <b>ornamental beards</b>, drawn-in eyebrows, <b>wigs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no \"filthy foreigner carrying who knows what\" into Pharaoh's presence</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:15-16</b>: \"no one can interpret... I heard you can\" - Joseph: \"<b>It is not in me</b>; God will give Pharaoh an <b>answer of peace</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"it'll be good\" (the baker!) - = <b>an answer that satisfies</b>: \"Yes, that's it\"</li><li class=\"d1\">other answers had been <b>unsatisfactory</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1688.88,"lv":2,"h":"41:17-24 - Pharaoh retells the dreams","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:17-24</b>: Pharaoh retells both dreams to Joseph</li><li class=\"d1\">cows came up out of the Nile; <b>ugliness \"never seen in all the land of Egypt\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">gaunt cows ate the fat; <b>no one would have known</b> - still ugly; not fatter from eating</li><li class=\"d1\">thin ears devoured the good; \"no one who could explain it to me\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1758.9,"lv":2,"h":"41:25-32 - Joseph's interpretation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:25</b>: \"The dreams of Pharaoh are <b>one</b>. <b>God has shown Pharaoh what he is about to do</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Joseph doesn't say \"give me a couple days\" - <b>no deliberating</b></li><li class=\"d1\">image of the <b>change in prophecy</b>: Moses face to face, then prophets <b>speak for God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not vague inspiration - <b>God gives it</b> as he gave Pharaoh the dream</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:26-27</b>: good cows, good ears = <b>seven years</b>; thin cows, empty ears blighted by east wind = <b>seven years of famine</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:29-31</b>: <b>seven years of great plenty</b>, then <b>seven of famine</b>; plenty <b>forgotten</b>; famine <b>very severe</b></li><li class=\"d1\">famine <b>worse</b> than the plenty was good - devours all the prosperity</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:32</b>: dream <b>doubled</b> → <b>confirmation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a call to <b>repent</b>, not a threat - it <b>will</b> happen, regardless</li><li class=\"d1\">next <b>fourteen years</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1896.84,"lv":2,"h":"41:33-36 - Joseph's proposal","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:33</b>: Pharaoh to select a <b>sensible and intelligent man</b> over Egypt</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:34-36</b>: appoint <b>governors</b>; collect <b>one fifth</b> of produce in the plentiful years</li><li class=\"d1\">store grain <b>under Pharaoh's authority</b>, in the cities, as a <b>reserve</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"take <b>twenty percent</b>\" in abundance → surplus for the seven bad years</li><li class=\"d0\">\"You can now <b>prepare</b>\" - a trusted man in charge, with people under him in every city</li></ul>"},{"t":1971.16,"lv":2,"h":"41:37-41 - Pharaoh puts Joseph over Egypt","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:37-38</b>: advice good to Pharaoh and servants: \"can we find such a man... who has the <b>Spirit of God</b> in him?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">answer satisfies; gives him <b>peace</b></li><li class=\"d1\">to everyone: \"is there any guy <b>better</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:39-41</b>: \"God has shown you all this\" → no one as wise</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>over my house</b>; all my people ruled according to <b>your word</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"only in regard to the <b>throne</b> will I be greater than you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Like <b>Potiphar</b>, but for <b>all Egypt</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>emergency powers</b> for the coming crisis</li><li class=\"d1\">speaks on <b>Pharaoh's authority</b> - collects and stores grain city by city</li><li class=\"d1\">Joseph's path: Potiphar → prison keeper → Pharaoh</li></ul>"},{"t":2090.06,"lv":3,"h":"Faithfulness honored; Egypt saved","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">He <b>stayed faithful</b> through \"more downs than ups\" - \"definitely an up\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Faithfulness = what <b>God honored</b> as a righteous man - same as <b>Abraham</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God <b>saving Egypt through Joseph</b></li><li class=\"d1\">promise to Abraham: <b>all the nations will bless themselves in you</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not exclusivist</b> - \"you and through you, everybody else\"</li><li class=\"d1\">a <b>pagan Gentile nation</b> saved through Joseph's faithfulness - hand in hand</li><li class=\"d0\">Prologue to the rest of Torah</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Exodus</b>: Israel created as a <b>kingdom of priests</b> - priests to the <b>nations</b></li><li class=\"d1\">nations blessed through Israel <b>only if Israel is faithful</b> - Joseph = example</li></ul>"},{"t":2238.88,"lv":2,"h":"41:42-45 - Signet ring, new name, wife","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:42</b>: <b>signet ring</b>, <b>fine linen</b>, <b>gold chain</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ring <b>seals documents</b> → when Joseph signs, <b>Pharaoh</b> signs: \"Pharaoh's signature, essentially\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:43-44</b>: second chariot, \"<b>bow the knee</b>\"; \"without your consent no man may lift his hand or foot\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:45</b>: named <b>Zaphenath-paneah</b>; wife <b>Asenath</b>, daughter of <b>Potiphera</b>, priest of <b>On</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"our second Potiphar,\" transliterated differently</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>On = Heliopolis</b> (later Greek name) - city of the <b>sun god Re</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Marries a <b>pagan priest's</b> daughter</li><li class=\"d1\">\"ethnic makeup\" of Israel - back to this in <b>Exodus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">famous apocryphal <b>Joseph and Asenath</b> - romance + her <b>conversion to Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d1\">popular with early Christians; <b>never scripture</b>; alluded to at the end of <b>Luke</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2413.4,"lv":3,"h":"Egyptian names and adoption","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: translation of Zaphenath-paneah? - Egyptian name → Hebrew → Greek → English; <b>no real translation</b>, theories, \"none super satisfactory\"; more next time</li><li class=\"d0\">Egyptian name = being <b>adopted into Pharaoh's household</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh clothes him - think of <b>Jacob giving the coat</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses</li><li class=\"d1\">\"drawn out of the water\" = <b>bogus etymology</b> - back in Exodus</li><li class=\"d1\">Moses = <b>child</b>, usually affixed to a <b>god's name</b>: <b>Ramses</b> = Re + Moses; <b>Thutmose</b> = Thoth + Moses</li><li class=\"d1\">Moses' name may have had a god's name <b>dropped</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sister <b>Miriam</b>: <b>Miriamni</b> = \"beloved of <b>Amun</b>\" - pagan god in it</li></ul>"},{"t":2608.28,"lv":2,"h":"41:46-52 - Seven plentiful years; two sons","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:46</b>: Joseph <b>30</b> when he stood before Pharaoh → now <b>37</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:47-49</b>: \"montage\" - travels Egypt setting up <b>warehouses</b></li><li class=\"d1\">gathered grain \"as the sand of the sea\" until he <b>stopped counting</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"just keep taking 20%... don't bother weighing it\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:50-52</b>: two sons by Asenath before the famine</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Manasseh</b> = <b>forgetfulness</b> - \"God made me forget all my troubles and my father's house\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Ephraim</b> = <b>fruitfulness</b> - \"fruitful in the land of my humiliation\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Hebrew names</b>, not Egyptian</li><li class=\"d1\">Manasseh firstborn; \"<b>switcheroo</b>\" in <b>chapter 48</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2726.29,"lv":2,"h":"41:53-57 - Famine begins","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:53-54</b>: seven years of plenty end; <b>famine</b> - \"in all lands, but in Egypt there was <b>bread</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>whole ancient Near East</b>, at least the <b>Levant</b> - but Egypt prepared because of the dream</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:55</b>: Egyptians cry to Pharaoh → \"<b>Go to Joseph</b>; whatever he says, do\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Joseph also runs <b>distribution</b> in all the cities</li><li class=\"d1\">not only nice clothes and honor - \"<b>working hard</b>\" - more faithfulness</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>41:56-57</b>: Joseph opened the storehouses; <b>all countries</b> came to buy grain</li><li class=\"d1\">\"earth\" = <b>land</b>: neighboring countries, not China</li><li class=\"d1\">\"you're the only ones who are prepared\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Sets up a <b>reunion</b> - next time</li><li class=\"d0\">\"We did three chapters\" - wrap</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next: the reunion with the brothers (Genesis 42)"});
